1
00:00:00,410 --> 00:00:01,810
(All characters, places,
and organizations are fictional.)

2
00:00:01,810 --> 00:00:03,240
(Children and teens were filmed
under production guidelines.)

3
00:00:05,440 --> 00:00:06,850
Mom?

4
00:00:08,950 --> 00:00:09,950
Mom?

5
00:00:23,860 --> 00:00:25,000
Is that your mother, Manager Kang?

6
00:00:26,060 --> 00:00:27,670
Yes. Have a good evening, ma'am.

7
00:00:28,870 --> 00:00:30,570
All right. Good work.

8
00:00:40,410 --> 00:00:41,410
Mom.

9
00:00:42,480 --> 00:00:44,080
Sweetheart, are you okay?

10
00:00:45,220 --> 00:00:46,550
What brings you all the way here?

11
00:00:47,290 --> 00:00:49,020
I came because I missed my daughter.

12
00:00:50,790 --> 00:00:51,960
By the way, who was that?

13
00:00:53,090 --> 00:00:55,360
From what I saw,
it looked like she was scolding you.

14
00:00:56,430 --> 00:00:57,800
She's the CEO of our company.

15
00:00:59,200 --> 00:01:01,030
She was just saying
I worked hard overtime.

16
00:01:02,900 --> 00:01:05,370
You should've called.
Have you been waiting long?

17
00:01:05,800 --> 00:01:08,340
No. Did you eat?

18
00:01:09,410 --> 00:01:11,080
Are you eating dinner while working?

19
00:01:12,680 --> 00:01:15,480
Of course. When have you ever seen
your daughter skip a meal?

20
00:01:17,450 --> 00:01:20,420
Mom, you look gorgeous
in that yellow dress!

21
00:01:20,820 --> 00:01:22,150
- Really?
- Yes.

22
00:01:25,990 --> 00:01:27,290
Mom, sit here.

23
00:01:28,060 --> 00:01:29,830
Everything else looks fine, but...

24
00:01:30,560 --> 00:01:32,400
since it's a rooftop room,
it must get hot in the summer.

25
00:01:32,730 --> 00:01:35,400
The air conditioner
and washing machine are so old.

26
00:01:36,570 --> 00:01:39,900
I asked Mi Seon,
and she said it works totally fine.

27
00:01:39,940 --> 00:01:42,040
If it breaks,
we can just get it fixed.

28
00:01:42,210 --> 00:01:43,610
Mom, sit down here.

29
00:01:43,680 --> 00:01:45,610
Are you inspecting the place
the minute you get here?

30
00:01:47,880 --> 00:01:50,680
At least you've been eating
the side dishes I packed for you.

31
00:01:58,360 --> 00:01:59,390
Mom.

32
00:01:59,560 --> 00:02:02,390
That man you went
to see the play with back then.

33
00:02:02,730 --> 00:02:04,430
Is he really just an acquaintance?

34
00:02:04,500 --> 00:02:05,560
What?

35
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:07,000
Oh, right.

36
00:02:07,500 --> 00:02:08,600
Why bring that up again?

37
00:02:09,600 --> 00:02:12,440
Are you two dating?

38
00:02:13,040 --> 00:02:15,740
Come on. Am I at an age for that?

39
00:02:16,070 --> 00:02:17,910
What does age have to do
with romance?

40
00:02:19,140 --> 00:02:23,780
By the way, you look so pretty.
I'll buy you another dress.

41
00:02:25,280 --> 00:02:27,750
Buy it when I get sick
of wearing this one.

42
00:02:29,250 --> 00:02:31,620
Hey, call Mi Seon and ask
when she's coming home.

43
00:02:32,220 --> 00:02:34,230
I need to feed her dinner.
She must be exhausted.

44
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:43,000
Here.

45
00:02:45,500 --> 00:02:46,500
Mother.

46
00:02:48,710 --> 00:02:51,880
You're not going to kick me out
for barging in unannounced, are you?

47
00:02:52,510 --> 00:02:53,710
Just let it slide for today.

48
00:02:54,910 --> 00:02:55,910
I'm glad you came.

49
00:02:56,450 --> 00:02:58,050
Did you come because
you were worried about Da Mi?

50
00:02:58,620 --> 00:03:01,850
Please eat.
I'll make you a meal for once.

51
00:03:02,190 --> 00:03:03,590
I'll do it.

52
00:03:03,590 --> 00:03:04,860
You took Da Mi in,

53
00:03:04,860 --> 00:03:06,390
and even feed her,

54
00:03:06,660 --> 00:03:08,190
so let me return the favor, dear.

55
00:03:09,430 --> 00:03:10,630
Compared to when I lived alone,

56
00:03:10,630 --> 00:03:11,860
I'm much happier living
with Da Mi...

57
00:03:12,760 --> 00:03:14,130
because I don't feel lonely anymore.

58
00:03:19,500 --> 00:03:20,610
You're back, Ma'am?

59
00:03:21,340 --> 00:03:23,470
- Where's Mother?
- She's in her room.

60
00:03:23,710 --> 00:03:25,610
She said she was going
to take a nap.

61
00:03:26,710 --> 00:03:28,750
Dr. Ju hasn't visited lately,
has he?

62
00:03:28,980 --> 00:03:31,120
No, he hasn't visited recently.

63
00:03:32,420 --> 00:03:34,890
Has she been taking
her medicine regularly?

64
00:03:35,420 --> 00:03:38,760
She doesn't take it in front of me.
I only bring her tea or water.

65
00:03:38,990 --> 00:03:41,430
She told me to leave,
saying she'd take it herself.

66
00:03:42,790 --> 00:03:43,800
Is that so?

67
00:03:46,900 --> 00:03:47,900
You are late.

68
00:03:48,400 --> 00:03:49,500
I am sorry, honey.

69
00:03:51,170 --> 00:03:53,710
I was reading a book,
so I didn't even hear you come in.

70
00:03:55,370 --> 00:03:56,370
It's all right.

71
00:03:58,510 --> 00:03:59,510
Honey.

72
00:03:59,980 --> 00:04:04,050
Have you ever seen
your mother take her medicine?

73
00:04:04,750 --> 00:04:05,750
Her medicine?

74
00:04:06,280 --> 00:04:08,020
Yes, but why?

75
00:04:08,850 --> 00:04:10,590
Because I've never seen her take it.

76
00:04:10,790 --> 00:04:13,090
Mrs. Anseong also said
she hasn't seen her take it either.

77
00:04:13,260 --> 00:04:14,260
I just found it strange.

78
00:04:15,390 --> 00:04:17,500
I wondered
what you were going to say.

79
00:04:17,800 --> 00:04:19,930
She takes it regularly,
so don't worry.

80
00:04:20,430 --> 00:04:22,000
When I took her tea,

81
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:23,330
I saw that she was
taking it diligently.

82
00:04:24,300 --> 00:04:25,540
In front of you?

83
00:04:26,340 --> 00:04:28,040
Yes, why?

84
00:04:28,640 --> 00:04:29,740
Are you worried...

85
00:04:29,810 --> 00:04:30,880
she might skip it
because it's a hassle?

86
00:04:33,440 --> 00:04:36,480
I'm relieved her mind
has been clearer lately,

87
00:04:37,080 --> 00:04:39,350
but if she keeps insisting
on taking it alone,

88
00:04:39,820 --> 00:04:41,620
what if she forgets to take it?

89
00:04:42,720 --> 00:04:44,990
Yes, I was just suddenly worried.

90
00:04:46,490 --> 00:04:48,390
Ever since Seung Yun moved in,

91
00:04:48,790 --> 00:04:51,330
she definitely seems
to be getting better.

92
00:04:52,600 --> 00:04:54,170
What a relief.

93
00:04:59,840 --> 00:05:02,770
Yes, I'm sure it's a relief to you.

94
00:05:13,450 --> 00:05:16,490
It tastes even better
when you serve it, Mother.

95
00:05:17,660 --> 00:05:21,090
Well, my mom's cooking
is the best in the world.

96
00:05:21,760 --> 00:05:24,630
What is with you two?
You are flattering me too much.

97
00:05:30,670 --> 00:05:31,900
By the way, Mother.

98
00:05:32,500 --> 00:05:33,500
Yes?

99
00:05:34,110 --> 00:05:37,510
Lately, your face looks
much more gaunt than before.

100
00:05:38,140 --> 00:05:39,380
Don't you think so, Da Mi?

101
00:05:41,580 --> 00:05:42,680
Do you think so?

102
00:05:43,450 --> 00:05:44,750
Did you lose weight, Mom?

103
00:05:45,880 --> 00:05:48,720
No, it's the same.

104
00:05:50,050 --> 00:05:51,290
I'm wearing clothes
I don't usually wear,

105
00:05:51,360 --> 00:05:52,720
so it must just look that way.

106
00:05:56,190 --> 00:05:57,230
Hurry up and eat.

107
00:06:03,940 --> 00:06:06,040
Are you just getting here?
I got here a little while ago.

108
00:06:06,500 --> 00:06:07,510
Yes.

109
00:06:08,010 --> 00:06:09,040
Hey, by the way,

110
00:06:11,410 --> 00:06:13,140
there's something
I need to tell you, Do Yun.

111
00:06:14,280 --> 00:06:15,280
What is it?

112
00:06:15,450 --> 00:06:16,850
From now on,
when Kang Da Mi is around,

113
00:06:16,910 --> 00:06:17,920
don't order fried chicken.

114
00:06:18,220 --> 00:06:20,050
Better yet,
don't even bring up fried chicken.

115
00:06:21,750 --> 00:06:23,120
I asked her,

116
00:06:23,620 --> 00:06:25,490
and she said she doesn't
really like fried chicken.

117
00:06:26,190 --> 00:06:28,430
Everyone has at least
one thing like that, you know.

118
00:06:28,630 --> 00:06:29,760
A food they dislike or something.

119
00:06:30,090 --> 00:06:31,130
Actually, I heard too.

120
00:06:32,560 --> 00:06:34,470
- What?
- What Da Mi said.

121
00:06:35,100 --> 00:06:36,330
Earlier, neither of you
were coming down,

122
00:06:36,400 --> 00:06:37,770
so I went up to the rooftop
looking for you.

123
00:06:40,670 --> 00:06:42,640
- You heard everything?
- Yes.

124
00:06:42,710 --> 00:06:45,380
It felt awkward to interrupt,
so I just came right back down.

125
00:06:46,010 --> 00:06:47,650
I couldn't just butt in
on a talk like that.

126
00:06:48,080 --> 00:06:49,150
I see.

127
00:06:51,050 --> 00:06:52,050
Good call.

128
00:06:52,880 --> 00:06:54,650
Then neither of us
should mention this...

129
00:06:54,650 --> 00:06:56,190
to Kang Da Mi from now on.

130
00:06:56,550 --> 00:06:59,160
- Not until she brings it up first.
- Yes.

131
00:06:59,390 --> 00:07:00,460
The good thing is...

132
00:07:00,990 --> 00:07:03,330
I was also raised
with lots of love by my mom.

133
00:07:04,030 --> 00:07:05,460
So I really felt for her.

134
00:07:06,600 --> 00:07:10,000
Da Mi turned out so well too.
She's always so cheerful, confident,

135
00:07:10,330 --> 00:07:11,770
and so kind to everyone.

136
00:07:13,070 --> 00:07:14,570
Still, hearing that fried chicken
reminds her...

137
00:07:14,870 --> 00:07:16,770
of being abandoned
by her birth mother...

138
00:07:17,540 --> 00:07:18,610
really breaks my heart.

139
00:07:20,310 --> 00:07:21,680
Who are you talking about, Do Yun?

140
00:07:24,080 --> 00:07:25,150
What do you mean, birth mother?

141
00:07:25,680 --> 00:07:27,890
Who on earth are you two
talking about so intensely?

142
00:07:28,390 --> 00:07:30,020
- Well...
- It's nothing.

143
00:07:30,090 --> 00:07:31,290
I will excuse myself now.

144
00:07:47,210 --> 00:07:49,840
Why are you so curious?
It's really nothing, Mom.

145
00:07:50,170 --> 00:07:51,340
What is it?

146
00:07:51,880 --> 00:07:53,980
The more you avoid it,
the more curious I get.

147
00:07:55,680 --> 00:07:58,420
Were you talking about Kang Da Mi?

148
00:07:58,420 --> 00:08:01,090
Nothing gets past you, Mom.

149
00:08:01,990 --> 00:08:03,150
Yes, that's right.

150
00:08:03,650 --> 00:08:04,760
I knew it.

151
00:08:06,220 --> 00:08:10,230
Do Yun, honestly, earlier today,
my feelings were a little hurt.

152
00:08:11,560 --> 00:08:13,760
- Why?
- In my own way,

153
00:08:14,270 --> 00:08:17,600
in that crisis,
I was grateful to Kang Da Mi...

154
00:08:17,670 --> 00:08:21,840
for coming up with a great idea,
and I wanted to encourage her.

155
00:08:22,310 --> 00:08:24,440
That's why I went down with snacks.

156
00:08:24,710 --> 00:08:27,480
But when she turned it down
and avoided me,

157
00:08:28,110 --> 00:08:30,080
I was a bit taken aback.

158
00:08:30,750 --> 00:08:33,850
Look, Mom.
She didn't refuse it because of you.

159
00:08:34,090 --> 00:08:36,290
- Please don't get the wrong idea.
- The wrong idea?

160
00:08:36,650 --> 00:08:38,360
Yes, it turns out Da Mi...

161
00:08:39,060 --> 00:08:40,890
was raised by a stepmother too.

162
00:08:41,960 --> 00:08:44,860
Then did her birth mother
pass away when she was young?

163
00:08:45,960 --> 00:08:47,030
It's not that.

164
00:08:47,770 --> 00:08:50,400
She was abandoned as a child.

165
00:08:51,840 --> 00:08:52,840
What?

166
00:08:53,270 --> 00:08:54,440
She was abandoned.

167
00:08:54,440 --> 00:08:55,870
And on that day,

168
00:08:56,340 --> 00:08:58,340
the last thing her birth mother
bought for her...

169
00:08:58,410 --> 00:08:59,410
was fried chicken.

170
00:09:01,080 --> 00:09:02,450
That's why she can't eat it.

171
00:09:02,450 --> 00:09:03,750
Because of childhood trauma.

172
00:09:05,580 --> 00:09:06,580
I felt so bad for her.

173
00:09:09,320 --> 00:09:10,820
She's always so cheerful,
I had no idea...

174
00:09:10,890 --> 00:09:11,890
she had a past like that.

175
00:09:13,760 --> 00:09:14,760
Wait.

176
00:09:14,890 --> 00:09:18,130
Are you two already close enough...

177
00:09:18,730 --> 00:09:20,300
for her to share
such personal things with you?

178
00:09:20,930 --> 00:09:23,270
No, I just happened to overhear.

179
00:09:23,630 --> 00:09:24,670
So...

180
00:09:25,500 --> 00:09:26,840
please pretend you don't know.

181
00:09:27,000 --> 00:09:29,570
- And don't take it the wrong way.
- Of course I won't.

182
00:09:29,970 --> 00:09:32,180
Thanks for telling me, Do Yun.
Get some rest.

183
00:09:32,740 --> 00:09:33,980
Okay. Good night, Mom.

184
00:09:57,870 --> 00:09:59,440
Mom?

185
00:10:09,610 --> 00:10:11,550
Then that woman earlier
wasn't her biological mother,

186
00:10:11,550 --> 00:10:12,980
and she's her adoptive mother.

187
00:10:15,490 --> 00:10:17,050
The day she was abandoned,

188
00:10:17,560 --> 00:10:19,360
her biological mother
bought her fried chicken?

189
00:10:22,260 --> 00:10:23,260
Eat up, hurry.

190
00:10:24,700 --> 00:10:26,460
You begged for fried chicken
for days,

191
00:10:26,530 --> 00:10:27,800
so why aren't you eating?

192
00:10:28,730 --> 00:10:31,000
Mom, what about Great-Aunt?

193
00:10:32,000 --> 00:10:34,210
Great-Aunt likes fried chicken too.

194
00:10:35,440 --> 00:10:37,210
She's unpacking, I told you.

195
00:10:38,310 --> 00:10:39,440
Just hurry and eat.

196
00:10:41,980 --> 00:10:45,120
No way. No, it couldn't be...

197
00:10:47,550 --> 00:10:49,850
Why did it have to be
fried chicken for her too?

198
00:10:51,260 --> 00:10:52,520
This is unsettling.

199
00:10:54,890 --> 00:10:55,960
That's refreshing.

200
00:10:56,590 --> 00:10:58,130
- Feels good.
- Grandma.

201
00:10:59,000 --> 00:11:01,830
If a debtor suddenly dies,

202
00:11:02,670 --> 00:11:03,930
what happens to me?

203
00:11:04,200 --> 00:11:07,840
Did Kang Dae Chi say
he was going to die?

204
00:11:08,440 --> 00:11:10,470
Because you've been hounding him
so much?

205
00:11:11,180 --> 00:11:13,240
I don't think that's it.

206
00:11:14,150 --> 00:11:16,080
Anyway, I just have a bad feeling.

207
00:11:16,780 --> 00:11:18,850
Grandma. I take after you,

208
00:11:18,920 --> 00:11:20,250
so you know my gut feeling
is spot-on, right?

209
00:11:21,620 --> 00:11:23,420
Can't you help me out a bit?
Please, Grandma.

210
00:11:24,420 --> 00:11:26,790
- No.
- What?

211
00:11:27,190 --> 00:11:28,830
Why, Grandma?

212
00:11:29,060 --> 00:11:32,000
What if something terrible
really happens?

213
00:11:32,700 --> 00:11:35,530
As if racking up debts
left and right weren't enough,

214
00:11:35,600 --> 00:11:38,700
he even got fired from his job.
Good grief.

215
00:11:38,770 --> 00:11:42,470
I looked into everything.
What a worthless fellow.

216
00:11:43,910 --> 00:11:48,350
He was fired unfairly.
And his money was stolen in a scam.

217
00:11:48,880 --> 00:11:50,050
What?

218
00:11:50,410 --> 00:11:52,180
Is that what Kang Dae Chi told you?

219
00:11:52,820 --> 00:11:54,450
And you actually believe him?

220
00:11:55,450 --> 00:11:57,890
I mean, my debtor
is chasing after the scammer...

221
00:11:57,890 --> 00:11:59,360
to catch him right now.

222
00:12:00,360 --> 00:12:03,060
But something must have happened
while chasing...

223
00:12:03,690 --> 00:12:05,730
because his voice over the phone
sounded like...

224
00:12:06,030 --> 00:12:07,500
he wanted to give up on everything.

225
00:12:07,800 --> 00:12:12,540
- Well, what did he say exactly?
- He said it's all over for him now.

226
00:12:13,370 --> 00:12:16,310
Even when I asked where he was
and said I'd come right away,

227
00:12:16,410 --> 00:12:18,740
he said he'd come himself,
and then he just hung up.

228
00:12:19,240 --> 00:12:20,780
He won't answer his phone
anymore either.

229
00:12:22,550 --> 00:12:24,010
Please help, Grandma.

230
00:12:24,680 --> 00:12:26,020
We need to keep him alive...

231
00:12:26,180 --> 00:12:27,920
so you can get
your money back too, right?

232
00:12:28,820 --> 00:12:29,890
Am I wrong?

233
00:12:32,860 --> 00:12:34,020
Just this once.

234
00:12:34,960 --> 00:12:35,960
Please?

235
00:12:36,590 --> 00:12:37,600
I'm begging you.

236
00:12:59,980 --> 00:13:01,990
Why are you outside?
You'll catch a cold.

237
00:13:07,260 --> 00:13:08,360
Hey, Dae Chi.

238
00:13:09,830 --> 00:13:11,130
Why are you sitting
out here like this?

239
00:13:14,470 --> 00:13:15,700
You're home, Mom.

240
00:13:18,000 --> 00:13:20,000
Did something go wrong at work?

241
00:13:21,910 --> 00:13:22,910
No.

242
00:13:23,170 --> 00:13:25,040
If not, why the long face?

243
00:13:26,110 --> 00:13:27,610
The urgent matters
should have been taken care of already.

244
00:13:28,110 --> 00:13:30,410
I told you, even if it takes
years of steady work,

245
00:13:30,410 --> 00:13:32,950
you can pay off
the rest of the debt.

246
00:13:34,950 --> 00:13:35,950
Wait.

247
00:13:36,190 --> 00:13:37,660
Are you feeling sick too?

248
00:13:42,160 --> 00:13:43,490
You don't have a fever.

249
00:13:47,460 --> 00:13:48,870
I'm just exhausted.

250
00:13:51,540 --> 00:13:52,540
I'm going to my room.

251
00:14:02,880 --> 00:14:04,680
What am I going to do with you?

252
00:14:11,660 --> 00:14:14,120
You can't deny good genes.

253
00:14:14,260 --> 00:14:15,830
She's not only pretty...

254
00:14:16,330 --> 00:14:18,300
but also smart, just like her dad,

255
00:14:18,360 --> 00:14:20,100
which is why she works
at a big company.

256
00:14:24,670 --> 00:14:25,670
Mother.

257
00:14:26,470 --> 00:14:27,500
I'm home.

258
00:14:28,570 --> 00:14:29,570
Mi Mi.

259
00:14:36,210 --> 00:14:39,550
I didn't ask them to take this photo.
I really didn't.

260
00:14:40,080 --> 00:14:42,650
I said no,

261
00:14:42,650 --> 00:14:45,720
but that punk forced me into it.

262
00:14:49,190 --> 00:14:50,960
Why aren't you saying anything?

263
00:14:53,460 --> 00:14:55,000
What is there for me to say?

264
00:14:55,500 --> 00:14:57,770
You're just looking at a picture
of your own son.

265
00:14:59,870 --> 00:15:01,610
You don't have to hide it anymore.

266
00:15:02,340 --> 00:15:03,670
Don't sneak around like that.

267
00:15:04,280 --> 00:15:06,910
Even a beast has some shame.

268
00:15:07,480 --> 00:15:09,780
Under your roof,
right in front of you,

269
00:15:10,450 --> 00:15:11,950
how could I do that?

270
00:15:12,680 --> 00:15:14,290
I'm fine, Mother.

271
00:15:15,090 --> 00:15:17,390
It hurts me more...

272
00:15:18,060 --> 00:15:20,360
to see you hiding it behind my back.

273
00:15:21,490 --> 00:15:22,530
I mean it.

274
00:15:29,900 --> 00:15:31,170
"Fine," my foot.

275
00:15:32,540 --> 00:15:34,410
Do you think I don't know
how you feel?

276
00:15:35,710 --> 00:15:37,740
That miserable punk.

277
00:15:38,710 --> 00:15:40,240
If only I could just cut
all ties of blood with him...

278
00:15:40,310 --> 00:15:43,380
like slicing through a radish...

279
00:15:51,760 --> 00:15:52,760
Hey.

280
00:15:53,890 --> 00:15:55,030
What are you doing?

281
00:15:55,690 --> 00:15:56,790
You're back, Mi Mi.

282
00:15:57,930 --> 00:16:00,900
What do you think?
Don't these look better on me?

283
00:16:01,870 --> 00:16:04,370
I do have petite,
pretty feet, you know.

284
00:16:04,900 --> 00:16:07,440
Even if they're new shoes,

285
00:16:07,540 --> 00:16:09,140
why keep them
enshrined in your room?

286
00:16:10,310 --> 00:16:11,310
Take them off.

287
00:16:12,540 --> 00:16:13,540
What?

288
00:16:13,580 --> 00:16:16,110
Take them off right now.
Those are mine.

289
00:16:16,350 --> 00:16:18,180
Come on.

290
00:16:18,380 --> 00:16:20,380
Since when do we draw lines
over what's yours and mine?

291
00:16:20,450 --> 00:16:21,890
Why are you getting so serious?

292
00:16:22,690 --> 00:16:26,790
Hey, let me borrow these sometimes.

293
00:16:27,160 --> 00:16:28,860
I think I've been
overworking myself.

294
00:16:28,930 --> 00:16:33,660
Look at my skin, it's so ruined.
I should go get a vitamin IV drip.

295
00:16:33,730 --> 00:16:34,830
I really need one.

296
00:16:36,200 --> 00:16:37,940
Get an IV or drink it,
do whatever you want,

297
00:16:38,000 --> 00:16:39,040
just take them off.

298
00:16:42,510 --> 00:16:44,070
You're making such a fuss
over a pair of shoes.

299
00:16:44,410 --> 00:16:45,580
Fine.

300
00:16:55,150 --> 00:16:57,020
By the way...

301
00:16:58,090 --> 00:17:00,920
About that guy you were with.

302
00:17:01,890 --> 00:17:03,730
Gang Nam told me...

303
00:17:04,400 --> 00:17:06,860
he's really handsome
and looks young too.

304
00:17:07,460 --> 00:17:08,600
Who on earth is he?

305
00:17:09,100 --> 00:17:10,970
Just tell me, quietly.

306
00:17:13,070 --> 00:17:14,610
I swear I won't tell a soul.

307
00:17:14,940 --> 00:17:16,340
You expect me to believe
you'll keep your mouth shut?

308
00:17:16,340 --> 00:17:19,680
Yes, and your mother-in-law
is curious too.

309
00:17:20,510 --> 00:17:22,750
I really won't say a word.

310
00:17:22,750 --> 00:17:25,080
On our family's honor, I swear.

311
00:17:26,720 --> 00:17:27,990
Like I'd believe that!

312
00:17:28,520 --> 00:17:31,590
Why did you hit me?
Just use your words.

313
00:17:31,820 --> 00:17:33,460
As if you ever listen to me.

314
00:17:35,590 --> 00:17:37,090
I am tired. I am going to bed.

315
00:17:43,900 --> 00:17:47,070
She is as beautiful as ever,
my mother.

316
00:17:48,240 --> 00:17:51,510
This is all because Mi Mi
took such good care of her.

317
00:17:55,910 --> 00:17:57,210
What are you doing?
Aren't you leaving?

318
00:17:57,280 --> 00:18:00,420
I was looking at the photo
I took with Mother.

319
00:18:01,080 --> 00:18:03,390
You looked at it all night
before bed.

320
00:18:03,450 --> 00:18:04,460
You are going to wear it out.

321
00:18:06,120 --> 00:18:07,190
Honey.

322
00:18:07,860 --> 00:18:11,160
Let's get this photo
framed and hang it up.

323
00:18:11,800 --> 00:18:15,000
Just looking at it on my phone
leaves me wanting more.

324
00:18:16,170 --> 00:18:17,940
Sure, let's do that.

325
00:18:18,240 --> 00:18:20,340
When Mother visits
and sees the photo hanging up,

326
00:18:20,400 --> 00:18:22,340
- she will be thrilled.
- Right?

327
00:18:22,340 --> 00:18:24,140
We can show her that you're her son,

328
00:18:24,210 --> 00:18:25,440
I'm her daughter-in-law,
Ye Ri her grandchild,

329
00:18:25,510 --> 00:18:26,610
and that we are one family.

330
00:18:26,740 --> 00:18:28,910
We can show her
that we're one family.

331
00:18:32,320 --> 00:18:33,350
Show who what?

332
00:18:34,080 --> 00:18:36,490
Ye Ri, the photo
we took with Grandma.

333
00:18:36,650 --> 00:18:39,590
Could you order a print of it?
And get a matching frame, too.

334
00:18:39,820 --> 00:18:40,890
Okay, sure.

335
00:18:41,360 --> 00:18:44,830
Make sure
to pick the best-looking one, Ye Ri.

336
00:18:47,400 --> 00:18:50,630
Dad must be really happy
to see Grandma again, Mom.

337
00:18:51,470 --> 00:18:54,740
You should call Grandma
more often from now on.

338
00:18:55,610 --> 00:18:58,380
"Grandma, did you eat breakfast?"

339
00:18:58,380 --> 00:18:59,380
"It's so cold outside."

340
00:18:59,440 --> 00:19:01,310
"Make sure to dress warmly,
Grandma."

341
00:19:01,310 --> 00:19:03,650
Like that. Be affectionate.

342
00:19:03,650 --> 00:19:05,980
How can I do that all of a sudden?

343
00:19:06,050 --> 00:19:07,680
I only just met her.

344
00:19:09,020 --> 00:19:10,990
Do you know who she is?

345
00:19:11,190 --> 00:19:13,920
She is loaded.
She's a local big shot.

346
00:19:14,460 --> 00:19:15,530
Really?

347
00:19:16,060 --> 00:19:19,660
Yes, really.
So get on her good side.

348
00:19:20,030 --> 00:19:21,200
Do you hear me?

349
00:19:23,200 --> 00:19:27,240
Listen to yourself.
Are you saying if she had nothing,

350
00:19:27,300 --> 00:19:29,340
we shouldn't treat her well?

351
00:19:30,640 --> 00:19:33,040
Ye Ri,
treating her well isn't something...

352
00:19:33,040 --> 00:19:34,780
you do expecting something
in return.

353
00:19:35,050 --> 00:19:37,680
She is your grandmother.
It's only natural.

354
00:19:37,950 --> 00:19:38,950
Understood?

355
00:19:39,550 --> 00:19:41,620
- I'm heading out.
- Let's go together, Dad.

356
00:19:41,690 --> 00:19:43,150
I'm running late,
so you need to drive me.

357
00:19:43,220 --> 00:19:44,890
All right, let's go.

358
00:19:45,660 --> 00:19:46,660
Let's go.

359
00:19:49,160 --> 00:19:52,800
How much is Mother's estate worth
in total, anyway?

360
00:19:53,160 --> 00:19:54,770
I'm dying to know.

361
00:19:58,170 --> 00:19:59,740
(Mi Mi's Chicken Soup)

362
00:20:12,550 --> 00:20:13,820
Good morning, Dr. Ju.

363
00:20:14,750 --> 00:20:16,250
Are you heading to work already?

364
00:20:17,520 --> 00:20:19,220
Are you working again?

365
00:20:20,460 --> 00:20:22,290
I'm just prepping a few things.

366
00:20:22,960 --> 00:20:25,160
Without my touch,
things fall apart fast.

367
00:20:25,430 --> 00:20:26,760
Both the restaurant and the house.

368
00:20:29,100 --> 00:20:30,630
Welcome, Dr. Ju.

369
00:20:31,470 --> 00:20:33,070
Are you here for breakfast?

370
00:20:33,300 --> 00:20:34,840
Well... Ri Ja.

371
00:20:35,440 --> 00:20:36,470
Yes?

372
00:20:36,540 --> 00:20:39,480
Please make sure
your sister rests from now on.

373
00:20:39,680 --> 00:20:41,310
She must not overexert herself.

374
00:20:41,650 --> 00:20:42,650
Doctor.

375
00:20:43,810 --> 00:20:45,050
I am fine.

376
00:20:45,250 --> 00:20:47,080
I told you
I will rest right after prepping.

377
00:20:49,390 --> 00:20:52,220
As your physician,
I am giving you strict orders.

378
00:20:52,420 --> 00:20:53,790
You must get plenty of rest.

379
00:20:54,760 --> 00:20:56,030
Please look after her, Ri Ja.

380
00:21:03,430 --> 00:21:04,530
What was that?

381
00:21:04,700 --> 00:21:05,700
Just because
you had a stomachache...

382
00:21:05,700 --> 00:21:07,040
and visited the hospital
a few times,

383
00:21:07,040 --> 00:21:08,840
he is worrying about you like that?

384
00:21:10,470 --> 00:21:13,880
I mean,
it is not like you are a child.

385
00:21:14,280 --> 00:21:16,180
Even if he's your doctor,
that's a bit much.

386
00:21:17,710 --> 00:21:19,280
We have green onions to prep.
Get moving.

387
00:21:24,550 --> 00:21:26,560
(Ju Kyung Ho Internal Medicine)

388
00:21:26,820 --> 00:21:27,820
Hey.

389
00:21:32,100 --> 00:21:35,000
Could Dr. Ju have feelings for her?

390
00:21:36,430 --> 00:21:38,040
No way.

391
00:21:38,570 --> 00:21:39,700
He's probably
giving her special treatment...

392
00:21:39,700 --> 00:21:40,940
because she's the landlord.

393
00:21:50,450 --> 00:21:52,650
These are samples
by width and color for now.

394
00:21:55,190 --> 00:21:57,050
Please look them over...

395
00:21:57,050 --> 00:21:58,390
with the materials
and unit price sheet.

396
00:21:59,390 --> 00:22:01,360
This one matches best...

397
00:22:01,360 --> 00:22:03,290
with the sneakers
we plan to release.

398
00:22:04,590 --> 00:22:07,530
The texture is
definitely less coarse.

399
00:22:07,730 --> 00:22:09,800
- Want to feel it too, Kang Da Mi?
- Sure.

400
00:22:12,470 --> 00:22:14,910
This one looks good too.

401
00:22:15,870 --> 00:22:18,810
The material choice must align
with the unit price sheet.

402
00:22:19,110 --> 00:22:20,410
Since this is a promotional product,

403
00:22:20,480 --> 00:22:22,080
the retail price
must stay reasonable.

404
00:22:23,650 --> 00:22:28,090
Velcro is the best option,
but the price is the problem.

405
00:22:31,320 --> 00:22:32,420
It will be hard
to meet the target price.

406
00:22:33,660 --> 00:22:35,430
I was thinking the same thing.

407
00:22:35,930 --> 00:22:36,960
What should we do?

408
00:22:37,360 --> 00:22:39,860
The CEO told us to switch to Velcro.

409
00:22:43,930 --> 00:22:45,600
Kang Da Mi, do you have
any thoughts on this?

410
00:22:47,170 --> 00:22:50,510
Aside from the cost,

411
00:22:51,240 --> 00:22:55,410
seeing it in person makes it look
far more athletic than I expected.

412
00:22:56,350 --> 00:22:58,010
It looks like golf or bowling shoes,

413
00:22:58,010 --> 00:23:01,280
so wearing them with a skirt at work
feels a bit...

414
00:23:03,490 --> 00:23:05,890
Coming up with the Velcro idea
was your doing, Da Mi.

415
00:23:05,960 --> 00:23:08,530
Yes, I suggested it
as an alternative...

416
00:23:08,530 --> 00:23:10,160
to avoid the hassle of tying laces.

417
00:23:10,590 --> 00:23:11,700
Okay. So?

418
00:23:13,600 --> 00:23:17,500
Sneakers that keep the look of laces
without needing to be tied...

419
00:23:19,970 --> 00:23:21,240
Like an elastic band.

420
00:23:21,940 --> 00:23:24,470
What if we look into
elastic lace materials?

421
00:23:24,640 --> 00:23:26,780
That way, people can just slip
their feet in and out.

422
00:23:27,380 --> 00:23:29,310
Elastic laces?

423
00:23:30,080 --> 00:23:31,880
Yes, they stretch automatically,

424
00:23:31,880 --> 00:23:34,620
so they will hold the foot securely
without pinching the instep.

425
00:23:35,290 --> 00:23:37,450
And we don't need
to change the design much.

426
00:23:37,450 --> 00:23:40,990
Then we must check its stretch
and recovery strength.

427
00:23:40,990 --> 00:23:42,530
It cannot stretch out too easily.

428
00:23:43,760 --> 00:23:44,800
Sounds good.

429
00:23:45,300 --> 00:23:46,730
Let us contact the supplier
right away...

430
00:23:46,730 --> 00:23:48,000
and make another sample.

431
00:23:49,270 --> 00:23:51,870
Da Mi, you are like an idea
vending machine.

432
00:23:52,670 --> 00:23:53,670
You are on a roll.

433
00:23:54,840 --> 00:23:57,610
Indeed. You are a big help, Da Mi.

434
00:24:01,980 --> 00:24:04,820
What?
Am I supposed to praise you too?

435
00:24:04,950 --> 00:24:06,150
It is just your job anyway.

436
00:24:07,680 --> 00:24:09,490
I did not say anything.

437
00:24:10,020 --> 00:24:11,050
Right.

438
00:24:19,060 --> 00:24:20,060
Welcome...

439
00:24:23,230 --> 00:24:24,400
What are you doing?

440
00:24:27,400 --> 00:24:28,770
You are here, Ri Ja?

441
00:24:29,540 --> 00:24:30,540
What brings you?

442
00:24:30,910 --> 00:24:32,210
Did you think I came to see you?

443
00:24:32,980 --> 00:24:34,140
Dr. Ju is in, right?

444
00:24:34,540 --> 00:24:37,510
He stepped out. He said
he had something important.

445
00:24:39,250 --> 00:24:40,750
By the way, what is this container?

446
00:24:41,320 --> 00:24:42,790
It is radish kimchi, right?

447
00:24:43,350 --> 00:24:46,020
Did you make it? For Dr. Ju?

448
00:24:46,820 --> 00:24:51,060
You are just as much of an airhead now
as you were back then.

449
00:25:03,840 --> 00:25:05,440
When he gets back,

450
00:25:05,640 --> 00:25:08,980
make sure you tell him I brought it.
Got it?

451
00:25:15,550 --> 00:25:16,620
Look at you cowering.

452
00:25:17,220 --> 00:25:20,320
I am holding back
only because of my sister,

453
00:25:20,860 --> 00:25:21,930
so watch yourself.

454
00:25:23,590 --> 00:25:24,590
See you around.

455
00:25:30,100 --> 00:25:32,570
Did she just say, "See you around?"
Poor me.

456
00:25:42,780 --> 00:25:45,450
What is wrong, sweetheart?
You even skipped your ice pop today.

457
00:25:46,120 --> 00:25:47,180
Do you feel sick?

458
00:25:47,520 --> 00:25:49,790
Dad, I do not want
to go to kindergarten.

459
00:25:50,390 --> 00:25:53,820
- I do not want to go.
- Why so suddenly?

460
00:25:54,360 --> 00:25:56,460
I just do not want to go anymore.

461
00:26:00,930 --> 00:26:02,200
Did you fight with a friend?

462
00:26:02,770 --> 00:26:05,170
Or did your teacher scold you?

463
00:26:06,070 --> 00:26:07,100
No, it is not that.

464
00:26:07,470 --> 00:26:10,770
Su Ah, you are worrying Daddy.

465
00:26:11,470 --> 00:26:13,480
I really wish you would tell me.

466
00:26:17,250 --> 00:26:18,250
Su Ah.

467
00:26:19,080 --> 00:26:20,180
A family photo.

468
00:26:20,880 --> 00:26:22,020
A family photo?

469
00:26:22,650 --> 00:26:23,650
Yes.

470
00:26:24,020 --> 00:26:26,890
They told us to bring a family photo
with Mom and Dad.

471
00:26:27,520 --> 00:26:29,590
We are going
to make clay picture frames.

472
00:26:30,860 --> 00:26:33,060
But I do not have a mom.

473
00:26:34,200 --> 00:26:35,700
So I cannot bring one.

474
00:26:42,140 --> 00:26:43,140
Sweetheart.

475
00:26:44,140 --> 00:26:47,080
I told you to trust me, right?

476
00:26:48,980 --> 00:26:52,680
I'll make sure
you have a family photo to take.

477
00:26:53,180 --> 00:26:55,390
- Do not worry.
- Really?

478
00:26:55,920 --> 00:26:58,050
Yes, really.

479
00:27:02,190 --> 00:27:04,830
Please take a look here.
We are looking for someone.

480
00:27:05,360 --> 00:27:06,700
Excuse me, please take a look.

481
00:27:07,260 --> 00:27:08,370
Please take a look at this.

482
00:27:10,100 --> 00:27:11,100
Here.

483
00:27:11,200 --> 00:27:12,900
Please take a look.
We are looking for someone.

484
00:27:13,000 --> 00:27:14,070
(Missing Person)

485
00:27:14,140 --> 00:27:15,140
(Jeon Dam I, Age 5, Lost In 2002)

486
00:27:15,170 --> 00:27:16,410
(Please Help Find Our Family.
Reward Offered)

487
00:27:16,470 --> 00:27:17,570
(Lost 24 Years Ago)

488
00:27:17,640 --> 00:27:18,910
(Searching for Our Grandniece Dam I,
Age 5 in 2002)

489
00:27:21,480 --> 00:27:23,210
Here, please.
I'm looking for someone.

490
00:27:23,210 --> 00:27:25,020
- Please take a look.
- I'll visit the client myself,

491
00:27:25,080 --> 00:27:26,750
so why don't we grab a bite
around here first?

492
00:27:27,120 --> 00:27:28,150
Da Mi, are you hungry?

493
00:27:28,450 --> 00:27:31,550
- Yes, to be honest, I'm starving.
- Working in our field,

494
00:27:31,620 --> 00:27:34,720
you'll often miss meal times.
You'll have to get used to it.

495
00:27:35,230 --> 00:27:36,260
Okay.

496
00:27:36,860 --> 00:27:39,800
I'm starving too, Team Leader Cha.
What are we having?

497
00:27:40,300 --> 00:27:42,530
Well, it's customary...

498
00:27:42,600 --> 00:27:43,930
to let the newcomer
pick the lunch menu.

499
00:27:44,130 --> 00:27:45,240
Da Mi, you choose.

500
00:27:45,570 --> 00:27:46,570
What are you doing?

501
00:27:46,570 --> 00:27:48,910
- He said you pick the menu.
- Yes.

502
00:27:48,910 --> 00:27:50,110
Excuse me.

503
00:27:50,770 --> 00:27:51,940
Please take a look at this.

504
00:27:52,010 --> 00:27:53,080
(Missing Person)

505
00:27:53,310 --> 00:27:54,410
I'm looking for someone.

506
00:27:54,680 --> 00:27:56,680
Yes. Just a moment.

507
00:27:57,110 --> 00:27:58,350
Kang Da Mi, hurry up.

508
00:27:58,980 --> 00:28:00,020
Yes, I'm coming.

509
00:28:03,690 --> 00:28:06,460
(Missing Person,
Jeon Dam I, Age 5, Lost In 2002)

510
00:28:10,760 --> 00:28:12,600
(Mission: Mompossible)

511
00:28:12,860 --> 00:28:15,500
How dare she hand out flyers
right in front of my company?

512
00:28:15,700 --> 00:28:17,370
You should've let me know
in advance.

513
00:28:17,700 --> 00:28:20,570
- No. Mother, please give it to me.
- I don't want to.

514
00:28:20,970 --> 00:28:23,510
Why do you keep being so nice to me?

515
00:28:23,510 --> 00:28:27,610
The one person who gave me
a reason to live is you.

516
00:28:27,910 --> 00:28:28,980
Who are you?

517
00:28:29,310 --> 00:28:30,310
I'm your father.

518
00:28:34,050 --> 00:28:36,050
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
